diagnosis_text:
The network between PC1 and PC2 is fully operational. Both hosts reside on the
same VLAN (VLAN 10) and the same IP subnet (10.1.0.0/24). PC1 is connected via
aswa2.eth0 (VLAN 10 access, PVID untagged) and PC2 via aswa3.eth0 (identical
configuration). Both access switches uplink to dswa1 with all STP ports in
forwarding state on the active path; the dswa2-facing uplinks on both aswa2 and
aswa3 are STP-blocked, which is correct and expected behaviour given dswa1's
lower bridge priority making it the root. dswa1's FDB for VLAN 10 shows PC1's
MAC learned on eth1 and PC2's MAC learned on eth2, confirming end-to-end L2
learning and forwarding is intact. A live ping from PC1 to PC2 returns 0%
packet loss with sub-2 ms latency, and traceroute confirms a single direct L2
hop — no routing is even involved. PC1's ARP cache holds PC2's MAC address
correctly. Neither host has any iptables rules, and dswa1's OSPF RIB correctly
installs 10.1.0.0/24 as a directly connected route. There is no injected fault,
no misconfiguration, and no degraded component anywhere on this path. The
user's report of an outage does not correspond to any verifiable network fault;
the complaint is a false premise. No corrective action is required.
